. LESSON 3 EDITING
. In these examples color 1 is teal, not red. $L1 says which of the
. palette's 256 colors color 1 shows (lesson 7); 29 is teal, and
. $L1=1 makes it red again.
$L1=29
. In the lesson you type EDIT TEST, and then these lines into the editor,
. and then change line 2. Here TEST is defined with the new line 2
. already in it. Type EDIT TEST to open it in the editor yourself.
TEST=[PR "THIS IS LINE 1"
PR "THIS IS THE NEW LINE 2"
PR "THIS IS LINE 3"]
TEST

. THE ANIMATION, and a macro to edit. SCANNER sweeps a bar back and
. forth, changing color at each end. Each step draws the bar in its new
. place first, then blacks out the strip it left behind, so the bar is
. always whole on the screen. Press ESC to stop it, type EDIT SCANNER,
. change the bar width 10, or D, the step, and run it again.
SCANNER=[CLEAR;X=0;D=2;C=1
X=X+D;BOX X,0,10,201,C;BOX X-3*D,0,D,201,0
IF X>150,D=-D;C=C\3+1
IF X<-150,D=-D;C=C\3+1
SKIP -3]
SCANNER
